    "intro_html":  "Porkolt is the Hungarian braise most Americans call goulash, and the secret is not the meat. It is the onions. There is nearly as much onion in this pot as there is pork, cooked down until it melts into the sauce and thickens it without a speck of flour. Potatoes cook right in the pot so there is no side dish to make, and it lands at 30 grams of protein for about $2.54.",
